    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0175" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg133"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 324.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 13, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received from Mr. Sprague, the
                    consul at Gibraltar, a telegram announcing that the Sumter left the port of
                    Gibraltar on the night of the 7th instant, in a very high wind, when it was
                    impossible to communicate with the Chippeway. He reports her as bound
                    westward.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
